To create, delete, and configure mail accounts, 
  the steps will depend on what mail server or 
control panel you are using — e.g., cPanel/WHM, \
Postfix + Dovecot, Microsoft Exchange, or others.

  ✅ Using cPanel (common in shared hosting environments)
1. Create a Mail Account
Login to cPanel.
Go to Email Accounts.
Click on Create.
Fill in:
Username (e.g., support@yourdomain.com)
Password
Mailbox Quota
Click Create.
2. Delete a Mail Account
Go to Email Accounts.
Find the email you want to delete.
Click the Delete button next to it.
3. Configure Mail Account (in Outlook, Thunderbird, etc.)
Find Mail Client Configuration in cPanel → Email Accounts → Connect Devices.
Use:
Incoming (IMAP/POP3):
Server: mail.yourdomain.com
Port: IMAP (993), POP3 (995)
Outgoing (SMTP):
Server: mail.yourdomain.com
Port: SMTP (465 or 587)
SSL: Enabled
Authentication: Yes (use full email address and password)

1. Create Mail User
Assuming mail domain is example.com:
sudo useradd -m support@example.com
sudo passwd support@example.com
